{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2193-08-06 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the surgical team. You're here today because you've been having trouble with fluid removal on peritoneal dialysis, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2193-08-06 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that's correct. I wasn’t getting enough volume off, and I was feeling bloated all the time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2193-08-06 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Because you're a rapid transporter, the peritoneal dialysis isn’t working as well for you. You’ve now switched to hemodialysis, which is going better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2193-08-06 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, much better. I feel more comfortable on hemodialysis. But I don’t need the old catheter anymore, so I’d like it removed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2193-08-06 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ve scheduled the removal for today. It’s a minor procedure, done under general anesthesia. Any questions before we go over the risks?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2193-08-06 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it safe with my heart condition and the mechanical valve?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2193-08-06 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good question. Because of your mechanical mitral valve, we need to manage your anticoagulation carefully. We’ll stop your warfarin and start a heparin drip after surgery to protect your valve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2193-08-06 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And then go back on warfarin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2193-08-06 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Once we’re sure there’s no bleeding, we’ll restart warfarin and monitor your INR closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2193-08-06 08:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. I’m ready to proceed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2193-08-06 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from surgery. The PD catheter was successfully removed. The procedure went smoothly, and you tolerated anesthesia well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2193-08-06 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I feel groggy, but okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2193-08-06 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Normal after anesthesia. We’ve started the heparin drip as planned to protect your heart valve. Your warfarin is paused for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2193-08-06 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds? I take tacrolimus and sirolimus for my transplants."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2193-08-06 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, those are continuing as usual. We checked your levels this morning—tacrolimus was 3.8, which is within range. No changes needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2193-08-06 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my blood work? I know my counts are usually low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2193-08-06 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hemoglobin is 10.0, which is stable. White count was low at 2.2, but we’ve seen that before. We’re watching it, but no sign of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2193-08-06 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. When can I start eating?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2193-08-06 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with clear liquids today. If you tolerate that, we’ll advance your diet tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2193-08-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You did well overnight—stable vitals, no pain at the incision site. We’re going to restart your warfarin today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2193-08-07 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the heparin still running?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2193-08-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the heparin will continue for now. We’ll overlap it with warfarin for a few days until your INR reaches the target."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2193-08-07 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should the INR be?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2193-08-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For your mechanical valve, we aim for 2.5 to 3.5. We’ll check it daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2193-08-07 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my dialysis? I’m used to my schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2193-08-07 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have a session tomorrow—planned for 2 liters of fluid removal. Then you’ll go back to your regular outpatient unit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2193-08-08 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your INR is 2.1 this morning. It’s starting to rise. We’ll keep you on 6 mg warfarin daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2193-08-08 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that close enough?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2193-08-08 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s moving in the right direction. We expect it to reach 3.0 by tomorrow. Once it’s stable, we can talk about discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2193-08-08 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d like to go home. I feel fine—walking, eating, no pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2193-08-08 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. We’ll plan for discharge tomorrow, assuming your INR is in range and you complete dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2193-08-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a bowel movement this morning—finally. I used the suppository and extra Miralax."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2193-08-08 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We were a bit concerned about constipation with the pain meds and reduced mobility. Good to see it’s resolving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2193-08-08 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I stop the heparin soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2193-08-08 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Once your INR is above 2.0 for two days, we’ll stop the heparin. That should be tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is 3.0 this morning—perfect. You’ve completed your dialysis session with 2 liters removed. You’re medically ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue all your usual medications, including warfarin 6 mg daily. The coagulation clinic will follow your INR."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the heparin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll discontinue the drip now that your INR is therapeutic. No need for it anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What signs should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call us if you develop a fever over 101, chills, or any redness, drainage, or bleeding at the incision site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And abdominal pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially worsening pain. Also, keep checking your INR as instructed and follow up with the clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll change the dressing daily, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Use clean technique and a new gauze each day. Let us know if it becomes wet or soiled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my dialysis schedule?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll resume your regular hemodialysis at your outpatient unit. They’ve been notified."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. We’ll arrange a chair car to take you home safely. Take care, and call if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your discharge papers are ready. The instructions are all written down, including follow-up contacts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ll review them when I get home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to leave once transport arrives. We’ll miss you, but this is a good step forward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It feels good to be going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve recovered well from the procedure and are in stable condition. We’re confident you’ll do fine at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll stay in touch with my doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best plan. Take care, and we’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2193-08-09 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're very welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2193-08-06 08:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2193-08-09 15:08:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 60-year-old woman with end-stage renal disease and a history of multiple transplants was admitted for removal of her peritoneal dialysis catheter due to inadequate volume clearance as a rapid transporter. She had transitioned to hemodialysis and elected to have the catheter removed. The procedure was performed on 2193-08-06 without complications. Postoperatively, she was started on a heparin drip for anticoagulation bridging due to her mechanical mitral valve. Warfarin was resumed the following day, and her INR rose from 2.1 to 3.0 by discharge. She tolerated diet, had a bowel movement with assistance, and completed a hemodialysis session with 2 liters of fluid removed. She remained stable, alert, and ambulatory throughout her stay. She was discharged home on her prior medications, including warfarin 6 mg daily, with instructions to follow up with the coagulation clinic and resume outpatient hemodialysis.",
    "problems": [
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Mechanical complication due to peritoneal dialysis catheter",
      "Kidney replaced by transplant",
      "Pancreas replaced by transplant",
      "Systolic heart failure, unspecified",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty status",
      "Heart valve replaced by other means",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Peripheral vascular disease, unspecified",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Personal history of tobacco use",
      "Kidney dialysis as the cause of abnormal reaction of patient, or of later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of procedure",
      "Accidents occurring in residential institution"
    ]
  }
}
